<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22022026</say-as>.</s> <s>It's twenty to four in the afternoon in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>The news.</s> <s>Nothing more.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Iran and the United States have set nuclear talks for early March, even as <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tɛˈrɑːn">Tehran</phoneme> hardens its <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="næˈtænz">Natanz</phoneme> facility and appoints a general to lead war preparations against a possible American strike.</s> <s>The sides remain far apart on sanctions, and American strike forces are expected in position by mid-March.</s> <s>These talks may be the last window for a diplomatic solution.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌsoʊmɑːliˈlænd">Somaliland</phoneme> has offered Washington lithium, coltan, and Red Sea military base access in exchange for diplomatic recognition.</s> <s>The unrecognized Horn of Africa territory is betting that American hunger for strategic minerals could finally tip the scales toward formal ties.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli settlers have seized five Palestinian-owned buildings in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈhɛbrən">Hebron</phoneme>, declaring a new settlement inside one of the West Bank's most contested cities without waiting for government approval.</s> <s>Fourteen nations condemned the move; settlers say they will not leave.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Brazil's President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈluːlə">Lula</phoneme> challenged Washington to treat all nations equally on tariffs, speaking from New Delhi where he signed critical minerals deals with Prime Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmoʊdi">Modi</phoneme>.</s> <s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈluːlə">Lula</phoneme> meets Trump next month with forty percent tariffs on Brazilian exports still in force.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Russia fired ballistic missiles and drones at <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈkiːɪv">Kyiv</phoneme> before dawn Saturday, damaging homes across five districts two days before the invasion's fourth anniversary.</s> <s>The war enters its fifth year on Monday with no ceasefire in sight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan struck Taliban camps inside Afghanistan across two provinces after a mosque bombing in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɪzˈlɑːməbɑːd">Islamabad</phoneme> killed thirty-one people.</s> <s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈkɑːbʊl">Kabul</phoneme> says the strikes killed civilians including children, and has threatened a response that could collapse the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈkɑːtɑːr">Qatar</phoneme>-brokered ceasefire.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indonesian forces evacuated seventy-five workers, including twenty-six Chinese nationals, from a <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈpæpjuə">Papua</phoneme> gold mine after armed separatists attacked a security post and killed two people.</s> <s>Military searches continue in a region where a decades-long independence movement rarely draws international attention.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Samsung has reclaimed the top spot in global memory chips, posting nineteen billion dollars in quarterly revenue and ending South Korean rival SK <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈhaɪnɪks">Hynix</phoneme>'s brief reign as market leader.</s> <s>Chinese state-backed chipmaker <say-as interpret-as="characters">CXMT</say-as> is undercutting with half-price chips, keeping pressure on the industry's dominant players.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>NASA has postponed the Artemis Two mission to April after a helium fault in the Space Launch System, delaying the first crewed Moon mission since Apollo.</s> <s>The setback puts at risk the agency's goal of landing astronauts on the Moon by 2028.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The Invisible Internet Project, a privacy network used by activists and journalists in censored countries, was overwhelmed by a botnet that outnumbered its nodes thirty-nine to one.</s> <s>Developers restored the network in six days, but the attack laid bare the fragility of decentralized privacy infrastructure.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We're back in three hours.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>